{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"8f9be22f-af6e-4174-b55b-e2d0553d0262","runId":"fe0ab98a-42d2-4bab-b97f-e38cec6dc7e2","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":13,"previousEventHash":"sha256:cac680be49446bdbb087c145bc78ae9d6248064c687060461129c6192cc37a38","type":"phase.completed","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a04374-6413-707f-bbd7-0dcfab4bb85a","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-27T13:46:35.352Z","idempotencyKey":"phase:investigate:1:complete","payload":{"phase":"investigate","attempt":1,"evidence":[],"report":"<!-- FORGE:INVESTIGATOR -->\n## Investigation Report\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Verdict | **Invalid** |\n| Confidence | **High** |\n| Severity | **High** if present; no current bypass observed |\n| Task Type | Production-safety regression validation |\n\n## What Was Claimed\n\nThe pnpm selector `--filter-prod` was allegedly omitted from selector detection, allowing `pnpm --filter-prod web test` to pass preflight against the root package and execute in another workspace.\n\n## What We Found\n\nThe frozen base contains no selector allowlist or `packageSelectionOption` helper. `packageScriptName` rejects every package-manager invocation whose first argument starts with `-`. Therefore `pnpm --filter-prod web test` reaches `unsupportedPackageManagerOptionsError` and cannot pass preflight. Existing focused coverage tests npm selectors but does not name pnpm `--filter-prod`, so a direct regression case is still warranted.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe source finding describes an earlier implementation. By frozen base `0b7fcd2c596e05d7a98e57a4464d39aae987f71d`, package-manager option handling had been generalized to fail closed before script inference, eliminating the cited omission.\n\n## Affected Files\n\n- `src/adapters/verification-preflight.ts` — current generic fail-closed package-manager option handling.\n- `test/adapters/verification-preflight.test.ts` — focused selector regression suite lacks the exact pnpm case.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `packageScriptName` throws whenever `argv[1].startsWith(\"-\")` for npm, pnpm, yarn, or bun.\n- No `packageSelectionOption`, selector list, or `--filter` token exists under `src/`.\n- Existing test coverage enumerates npm selector forms but not `pnpm --filter-prod web test`.\n\n## History Findings\n\nIssue #196 was created from correctness finding `correctness-argv-3` on PR #192 at head `d731df0c59a6c3bd3b36fcde512c759ab6625ae0`. The current frozen integration base instead uses generalized rejection, so the cited implementation is stale relative to this run.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nAdd the exact pnpm `--filter-prod` invocation to focused preflight regression coverage without changing production logic. This proves the current fail-closed invariant and prevents reintroduction of an incomplete selector list.\n\n## Related Issues\n\n- Source issue `#111`\n- Source PR `#192`\n\n## Decomposition Assessment\n\nNo decomposition is required. The remaining work is one focused test update.\n\n## Acceptance Spec\n\n- [ ] `pnpm --filter-prod web test` is rejected as an unsupported package-manager option.\n- [ ] The regression uses an available pnpm fixture executable so rejection exercises option validation, not executable lookup.\n- [ ] Required repository check passes.\n- [ ] Fresh correctness and security reviewers approve the frozen remediation head.\n\n<!-- INVESTIGATION:COMPLETE -->"}}
