{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"2a2b3f33-f8f5-42ca-a4d8-0a751ada7ed9","runId":"fe0ab98a-42d2-4bab-b97f-e38cec6dc7e2","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":19,"previousEventHash":"sha256:46aa4fe676f59842f0e495913d3c9e2575212b00123833f26b4f494174b76cbf","type":"effect.recorded","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a04374-6413-707f-bbd7-0dcfab4bb85a","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-27T13:48:05.470Z","idempotencyKey":"effect:github-label:RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi:196:d3d81763-1f3f-4498-bce5-4279464e3474","payload":{"effectType":"github-label","effectId":"github-label:RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi:196:d3d81763-1f3f-4498-bce5-4279464e3474","digest":"sha256:3a7d595f172d82aeba5f3d48b39757012dc0cda16094b06403a0b929178b9e59"}}
{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"df452e4d-ffdb-4132-b0c8-df7dfae703cc","runId":"fe0ab98a-42d2-4bab-b97f-e38cec6dc7e2","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":20,"previousEventHash":"sha256:cff87759ae97d7dda294947492bf3f3edaca72e0225cb7514a80c263fc71ccc7","type":"phase.completed","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a04374-6413-707f-bbd7-0dcfab4bb85a","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-27T13:48:48.432Z","idempotencyKey":"phase:plan:1:complete","payload":{"phase":"plan","attempt":1,"evidence":[],"report":"<!-- FORGE:CONTRACT -->\n## Builder Contract\n\n### Objective\n\nLock in fail-closed handling for pnpm `--filter-prod` by adding the exact reported invocation to verification-preflight regression coverage.\n\n### Allowed Paths\n\n- `test/adapters/verification-preflight.test.ts`\n\n### Forbidden Changes\n\n- Do not change production preflight behavior.\n- Do not change verification policy, command execution, workflow authority, schemas, or GitHub artifacts.\n- Do not add dependencies or broaden package-manager support.\n\n### Invariants\n\n- Package-manager options remain unsupported for tracked verification.\n- Rejection must occur after executable availability succeeds, proving option validation owns the failure.\n- Existing npm selector regressions remain intact.\n\n### Deliverables\n\n- An executable pnpm fixture alongside the existing npm fixture.\n- A focused `pnpm --filter-prod web test` regression case.\n- Passing required `check` verification.\n- Fresh correctness and security review of the committed head.\n\n### Acceptance Mapping\n\n| Check | Implementation |\n|---|---|\n| `AC-1` | Add `pnpm --filter-prod web test` to the malformed-root selector table and assert unsupported options. |\n| `AC-2` | Create an executable `pnpm` shim in the fixture PATH. |\n| `AC-3` | Run bound verification command `check`. |\n| `AC-4` | Prepare the PR and run the required fresh reviewer panel. |\n\n<!-- FORGE:CONTEXT -->\n## Implementation Context\n\n### History\n\nThe finding originated on PR #192 at head `d731df0c59a6c3bd3b36fcde512c759ab6625ae0`. Frozen base `0b7fcd2c596e05d7a98e57a4464d39aae987f71d` already replaced selector enumeration with generic rejection.\n\n### Callers And Data Flow\n\n`preflightRequiredVerificationCommands` resolves the executable, then `packageScriptName` classifies supported managers and rejects a leading option before package-script lookup. The test must supply pnpm on PATH to reach that branch.\n\n### CI Surface\n\nThe required bound command is `npm run check`, covering TypeScript compilation and all Node tests.\n\n### Prior Findings\n\nThe original high-severity production-safety concern was workspace selection escaping the configured cwd/package-script binding. Current source is safe; explicit regression coverage is absent.\n\n### Hazards\n\nA missing pnpm fixture would produce a false-positive test that only validates executable lookup. Production code changes would exceed the validated scope.\n\n<!-- FORGE:CONTEXT:COMPLETE -->\n\n<!-- FORGE:ARCHITECT -->\n## Implementation Plan\n\n1. Extend the test fixture to create an executable `pnpm` shim.\n2. Add the exact `pnpm --filter-prod web test` argv to the malformed-root selector regression table.\n3. Run required `check` verification and create the implementation commit.\n4. Prepare review and run fresh correctness and security reviewers against the frozen head.\n\n### Out Of Scope\n\n- Supporting package-manager selectors.\n- Refactoring preflight parsing.\n- Changing verification command execution or policy.\n\n<!-- FORGE:ARCHITECT:COMPLETE -->"}}
